    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0608" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg502"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Morgan to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Habana,
                                Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-11-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 259.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    between the department and this legation regarding the confiscation by Cuban
                    citizens of American registered trade-marks, concerning which representations
                    have been made to the department on several occasions by the Merchants’
                    Association of New York, I have the honor to inclose, in duplicate, for your
                    information, an article from the Havana Post of to-day’s date, regarding a
                    recent decision of the supreme court of Cuba, by which the owner of a foreign
                    patent is confirmed in the enjoyment of his patent rights in Cuba.</p>
                <p>It is not known whether this decision by implication may be interpreted as
                    protecting foreign trade-marks as well as patent rights.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin V. Morgan.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d443-a1.xml" xpointer="d443-a1"/>
            </div>
